# L §5.14.3: "Settlements are never measured. A move that binds over adjustments settles a change; a later version
# reaches what it settles through a new adjustment of the original instance, never by measuring the settlement, so
# the instance graph stays acyclic (P-8; ENGINE.md §5 step 2)". arr settles pay's adjustment by v2 (100.00 PLN); v3,
# known after arr's day, changes arr's amount (extra), yet no adjustment of arr is made: one adjustment, of pay, with
# change 100.00 PLN (the reality of L5_14_3_settle_adjusts_ends with extra added).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-02-28
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-03-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind pays: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place zus: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input extra: money PLN
input ok: bool
input d1: date
input d2: date
move pay: pays
  on d1
  when ok
  leg cash from zus to konto amount amt
move arr[a in adjustments on d2 where a.adjusts in pays]: pays
  on d2
  at a.day
  leg cash from a.adjusts.cash.from to a.adjusts.cash.to amount max(a.change, 0) + extra
  fulfils a
source s "x"
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100
  extra = 0
  ok = false
  d1 = 2026-01-05
  d2 = 2026-02-10
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-02-10
  replace ok = true
version v3
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-02-20
  replace extra = 5
ask n: count(true for a in adjustments over 2026), sum(a.change for a in adjustments over 2026) law cut
=== expect
n: (1, 100.00 PLN)
  law date 2026-02-28, cut 2026-02-28
